      "message": "[warning] Line 347: 🟡 `soleRemoteImage()` is intended to accept only a single-image HTML fragment, but the multiple-match rejection depends on `url.isValid()`. If the first `\u003cimg\u003e` has an invalid URL and a later one is valid, the function will still accept it. Track whether a match was already seen (independent of URL validity) and reject on any second `\u003cimg\u003e` to enforce the “sole image” contract reliably.",
